== S1 CT12: K=1, kappa=0, g=0, hold-last-value, exact reads ==
 mean error over cycle: T**(alpha - 1)*q/alpha
 T* = [(alpha*c/(q*w*(alpha - 1)))**(1/alpha)]
 matches CT12 T*: False
  elasticity of read rate in w: 1/alpha
  elasticity of read rate in q: 1/alpha
  elasticity of read rate in c: -1/alpha
 second derivative >0 (alpha>1): (2*T**alpha*q*w + alpha*(T**alpha*alpha*q*w - 3*T**alpha*q*w + 2*c))/(T**3*alpha)
 J* at alpha=2: sqrt(2)*sqrt(c)*sqrt(q)*sqrt(w)  (inventory sigma*sqrt(2cw) with q=sigma^2)
 CT13 penalty J(kT*)/J*: (q*w*(k*(1/(q*w*(alpha - 1)))**(1/alpha))**alpha + 1)/(k*(q*w*((1/(q*w*(alpha - 1)))**(1/alpha))**alpha + 1)) -> at a=2: (k**2 + 1)/(2*k)

== S2 CT7: read term re-priced per nat acquired (lam per nat), world sigma^2 random walk ==
 D* = sqrt(2)*sqrt(lambda)*sigma/(2*sqrt(w))  J* = sqrt(2)*sqrt(lambda)*sigma*sqrt(w)
 -> with lam=kT: sigma*sqrt(2 kT w). Note: this is a LOWER BOUND over trackers whose learning rate <= entropy production; it uses a per-nat price, not c_k*f_k per read.

